   "explain": {
    "en": {
     "text": "Communication sends a message from one point to another through a medium. Wired systems use metal wire or optical fibre. Wireless systems use radio waves, microwaves and infrared, which travel through air and even empty space at the speed of light. A transmitter puts the message on a wave; a receiver picks it up."
    },
    "am": {
